<!--main layout template where all other templates will be inserted

layouts are a way to avoid repeating the same HTML structure 
(like headers, footers, navigation bars) across multiple pages.
Instead of duplicating that boilerplate in every .ejs file, you define a
layout template and then “include” or “extend” it in your views.
app.engine("ejs", ejsMate);

layouts:Define a master template with placeholders (<percent- body %>). Each page extends the layout.
Includes: Insert reusable snippets (like navbar, footer, or form fields) into any template:
Layouts = master page structure (header, body).
Includes = reusable partials (navbar, form, footer).
  -->